OL,3,CRichard Tice: Reform UK deputy leader
OL,4,Cfacing parliamentary investigation
OL,6,FThe Reform UK deputy leader is facing
OL,7,Fa probe under rule six in the MPs'
OL,8,Fcode of conduct, which states that
OL,9,Fmembers must be "open and frank" in
OL,10,Fdeclaring "any relevant interest in
OL,11,Fany proceeding of the House or its
OL,12,Fcommittees", and in any communications
OL,13,Fwith public office-holders and public
OL,14,Fofficials.
OL,16,FTice claimed the inquiry is related to
OL,17,Fa complaint by an "anti-Israel
OL,18,Flobbying group" over whether he should
OL,19,Fhave referenced his register of
OL,20,Finterests at the start of "a debate on
OL,21,FUK democracy and Israeli influence".
